[1m[38;5;231mWhich task changes should generate a notification?[0m

  [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;114m[✔][39m Status changes
  [38;5;246mMoved to in-progress, done, blocked. The highest-signal event and the one people actually want.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m [38;5;114m[✔][39m Assignment changes
  [38;5;246mTask assigned to or reassigned away from someone. High signal, and it is how people get pulled into work.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m [38;5;114m[✔][39m Comments / discussion
  [38;5;246mSomeone said something on a task. High value for a collaborating team, and the most frequent event by volume.[39m
  [38;5;246m4.[39m [ ] Field edits
  [38;5;246mTitle, description, due date, priority. Lower signal, higher volume — the usual source of notification fatigue.[39m
